{
  "_note": "on_kerb: tyres verified on the photo to lie on the kerb (apex markers). height: per-barrier override of wall_height_m (apex markers are single tyres lying flat, onboard video 27.07.2026). Kerb style: stripes (default, red/yellow), apron (concrete pour painted red, then blue, with a white border by the grass - orthophoto 2026-04 and ground photos 2025-10; s_lower_outer is one too, not stripes), concrete (plain grey concrete pour); kerbs and pours are the climb from the asphalt to the verge grass 4 cm above it (pours rumble less: own APRON surface). behind: {style, width} = a second band between the kerb and the grass, at grass level, tapering with the kerb (s2_apex: the red / blue pour behind its stripes, 0.85 + 0.65 m measured on the 5 cm photo). stands: spectator benches along the start straight - benches = [s0, s1] metres along the line, each bench run traced on the 5 cm photo (runs of ~8 m, ~1 m apart, two rows of benches one behind the other up the bank, project author; seats ~0.45 m deep; three red planks on dark frames, Facebook photos); fence_offset = the 1.8 m wire mesh fence that far behind the bench line, away from the track (photo), a gap at the race control booth. paint: painted areas on the paddock (kind grid: two rows of 10 boxes, every other one mint, a blue pit strip between them, white outlines; kind line) traced on the 5 cm photo. buildings: footprint (from the roofs on the photos), height (storeys / shadows), facade (club = the plain white main building, annex = the single-storey annex in front of it, its wall to the paddock with the Kartodrom Gostyń sign and green stepped squares, booth, shed; roof = roof material; sign_edge = that wall, edge k joins points k and k+1; looks from the user's photo from the paddock), collision in 1WALL. boards: the timing board behind the last tyre pile on the left of the start straight (tyre_pile_east; project author), screen turned to the karts coming down the straight (aimed at the centreline 25 m before it). lamps: [x, y, height] from the round luminaires on the photo. stairs: from the paddock up to the stands bank, red / white railing both sides (project author); stairs north of the race control booth up the bank to the benches, red / white railing (drone close-up). The booth (drone close-up from the user): 3.2 m square, two storeys (5 m), the light blue door below and the cabin windows above to the track under a brown awning, grey flat roof; club, annex and booth repainted 2026: yellow walls, red where the green squares / bands / panels were (project author). Bench pairs alternate red / yellow. fences / gates: the corner behind the stands' south end (5 cm photo + Street View 2024, project author): the tall mesh fence closes the stands' end and runs down the bank to a galvanised field gate by the road, a low wire fence on posts carries on along the road (kind wire); collision in 1WALL. trees: [x, y, crown radius, height(, sprite 3 = conifer)] from the GUGiK surface model (NMPT, 0.5 m) minus the terrain: tree tops = local maxima of the canopy height, 3 m apart, crowns rough (flat roofs dropped, and red / bright roofs by their colour on the photo), height = canopy height at the top; the row by the west car park are conifers; 3D trees are four crossed alpha-tested planes (TREES, no physics). tyres: black = a row of plain black tyres (embankment_south: lying in one layer along the outside of the southern stretch, hand-traced on the 5 cm photo 2026-11-04), otherwise red / yellow blocks. Kerbs start at the asphalt edge = the painted white edge line; they narrow to a point at their ends over taper_m = [start, end] metres (driving order; default kerb_taper_m in track.json) - extents and tapers measured on the 5 cm photo 2026-11-04, width = paint incl. its white border. extra_asphalt: any simple polygon; on 2026-11-04 re-traced from the 5 cm photo (asphalt grown from the hand-traced plates, at most 2.5 m beyond them, stopping at grass, soil and 0.6 m inside the track asphalt); plates run on under the tyres standing on them (tyre_ring sits on connector_e, inside included); connector_e, divider_end and connector_ne are old shortcuts between two straights: each side is the rounded end of the grass island next to it (a )( shape: from the island tip a quarter ellipse to each track, fitted to the grass edge on the 5 cm photo), running 0.8 m under the track. grid: the painted grid pattern relative to the start line (first row first_m before it, rows row_m apart, the second column stagger_m further back, lateral_m = lane centres left of the centreline; `painted` boxes are drawn, AC_START slots beyond continue the pattern). painted_lines: lane lines at a constant offset from the centreline, from_m..to_m before the start line (negative = after it). Both fitted to the orthophoto 2026-11-03 (residuals < 0.1 m, lanes 2.11 m apart). painted_cross: dashed lines across the asphalt at_m before the start line (the lanes end on one 4 m after it). Traced by hand from the GUGiK orthophoto (build/cache/ortho.bmp) on a 5 m grid, ~0.5-1 m accuracy; on 2026-11-04 most tyre barriers were snapped onto their tyre rows on the 5 cm 2026 photo (ortho_near: brightness contrast of a tyre-wide band, kept only where it sits clearly better on the tyres) - not snapped: on_kerb ones, start_tyre_pile, hairpin_c_divider (already on the tyres), start_east, tyre_pile_east (not detected). Local metres (x east, y north) as in centerline.csv. Edit and re-run `build.py validate` - check build/ortho_overlay.svg.",
